                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I played it since 1999, and I think the sound track of this generation is the best in the series. It is also the first generation that introduces real-time battle mode. The battle field is much bigger, so you have enough room to outflank the enemy. As a defender, you can win by destroying the invader's HQ instead of eliminating them all. The AI of invader always give you chance by leaving just one unit to protect HQ and sending all others to attack city gate. By correspondingly sending all your units to raid invader's HQ, you can easily win any defense battle even you are outnumbered. So there is no danger of getting knocked out, and you can safely enjoy being a unenterprising monarch.\n\nThough there is no official translation, DIY is possible. The text data is stored in file \"message.s6\" in game directory, and it is a compressed file in ls11 format. After decompressing it, you can see the plain Japanese text files. And then you have a lot of localization works to do. I didn't say it's easy, I just said it's possible.\n\nIn fact, the gamer community has already done a great job on translation, and has created many new non-official mods for this game, in order to polish it as time goes by. So don't judge this game by it's graphics, it is more than it looks.",
